@NODE Background "EealDelete: Background and Purpose"
[------------( Background and Purpose )-----------------------------------]

The reason i wrote Eall-Deleter was becouse i am sick and tired of all
thoose old EALL messages that i no longer needed. Until this util was
born, i used EALL by Sigma Seven, but it was coded in AREXX and was really
slow and required alot of memory. (But the UTIL was really great!!)

NOTE: Take a look at the output example (Ealldelete.Output)

Greetings to SIGMA SEVEN!
@ENDNODE
@NODE Features "Ealldelete: Notable Features"
[------------( Notable Features )-----------------------------------------]

Several reasons to use EallDelete:

* Written entirely in C for fast code.
* Nice design.
* Fast! (Scans 2000 messages in 6 seconds)
* Scans the messagebase exactly the same way as amiexpress.
  (Check the included output example.)
* Special optimized versions for all CPU types.
@ENDNODE
@NODE Use "EallDelete: Install into Express"
[------------( How to use Eall Delete )-----------------------------------]

Eall Delete is really easy to use. It only requires one argument:

EALLDELETE <confpath>  - eg: EALLDELETE BBS:Elite/
                             EALLDELETE BBS:Conf1/  or whatever
@ENDNODE
